{"content":[{"c":["ELISHAMA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Ammihud’s son and leader of the Ephraimites at the beginning of the journey in the wilderness (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.10","r":"Num.1.10","rawR":"Num.1.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.10","value":"Num.1.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.18","r":"Num.2.18","rawR":"Num.2.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.18","value":"Num.2.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.48,53","r":"Num.7.48,53","rawR":"Num.7.48,53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.48,53","value":"Num.7.48,53"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:48, 53"},"). His was the ninth tribe in line during the wilderness march (",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.22","r":"Num.10.22","rawR":"Num.10.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.22","value":"Num.10.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:22"},"). Elishama was the father of Nun and grandfather of Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.26","r":"1Chr.7.26","rawR":"1Chr.7.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.26","value":"1Chr.7.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. One of David’s 13 sons born in Jerusalem to a legitimate wife (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.16","r":"2Sam.5.16","rawR":"2Sam.5.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.16","value":"2Sam.5.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 5:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.8","r":"1Chr.3.8","rawR":"1Chr.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.8","value":"1Chr.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.14.7","r":"1Chr.14.7","rawR":"1Chr.14.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.14.7","value":"1Chr.14.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Ishmael’s ancestor. Ishmael killed Gedaliah, the governor of Israel appointed by Nebuchadnezzar (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.25","r":"2Kgs.25.25","rawR":"2Kgs.25.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.25","value":"2Kgs.25.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.41.1","r":"Jer.41.1","rawR":"Jer.41.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.41.1","value":"Jer.41.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 41:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Man of Judah descended through Jerahmeel and Sheshan (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.41","r":"1Chr.2.41","rawR":"1Chr.2.41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.41","value":"1Chr.2.41"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:41"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Another of David’s sons (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.6","r":"1Chr.3.6","rawR":"1Chr.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.6","value":"1Chr.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:6"},"); alternately called Elishua in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.5.15","r":"2Sam.5.15","rawR":"2Sam.5.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.5.15","value":"2Sam.5.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 5:15"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.14.5","r":"1Chr.14.5","rawR":"1Chr.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.14.5","value":"1Chr.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 14:5"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Elishua_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Elishua_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Elishua_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Elishua"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Priest sent by Jehoshaphat to instruct the Judeans in the law of God (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.17.8","r":"2Chr.17.8","rawR":"2Chr.17.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.17.8","value":"2Chr.17.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 17:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["7. Prince and scribe in Jeremiah’s time (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.12","r":"Jer.36.12","rawR":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.12","value":"Jer.36.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:12"},"). He heard Baruch read the words of God, and later the scroll of the Lord remained in Elishama’s chamber until the king requested it to be read (vv ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.20-21","r":"Jer.36.20-21","rawR":"Jer.36.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.20-21","value":"Jer.36.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"20-21"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elishama","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 1:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.10","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.10","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.10"},{"anchorText":"2:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.18","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.18","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.18"},{"anchorText":"7:48, 53","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.7.48,53","rawQueryValue":"Num.7.48,53","sourceRefExact":"Num.7.48,53"},{"anchorText":"10:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.22","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.22","sourceRefExact":"Num.10.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.26","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.26","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.26"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 5:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.16","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.16","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.8"},{"anchorText":"14:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.14.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.14.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.14.7"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 25:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.25.25","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.25.25","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.25.25"},{"anchorText":"Jer 41:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.41.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.41.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.41.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.41"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.6","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.6","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.6"},{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 5:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.5.15","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.5.15","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.5.15"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.14.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.14.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.14.5"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 17:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.17.8","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.17.8","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.17.8"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.12","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.12"},{"anchorText":"20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.20-21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2e8f19836d5448cab00c038557b7acd139463caa8431869791d4849168841ba9","sourceItemName":"Elishama","sourceItemOrder":115,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elishama","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elishama","title":"Elishama","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}